+# HR corridors clamped to watch zones: fix in `gen.py`
+
+## Cause
+
+`hr_target()` in `gen.py` emitted every HR corridor as
+`{"units": "%lthr", "value": lo, "end": hi}`. The API accepts that shape and
+returns it unchanged (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`), so the problem is
+not visible in the readback. Per the colleague's note, Intervals exports a
+target keyed by `value` as a zone-mapped (lap-HR) target, and the watch clamps
+that to its own LTHR zones. That matches what the watch showed: every corridor
+landed on a zone edge (118–137, 137–151, 151–162) rather than 151–160 or
+129–141.
+
+## Change
+
+`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: the corridor is now
+`{"units": "%lthr", "start": lo, "end": hi}`. The docstring records why `start`
+is used, so nobody changes it back to `value` later.
+
+Checked by running `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json`: all four corridors
+now carry `start`/`end`, and no `value` keys remain. The percentages (68–75,
+88–93, 75–82, 65–72) are unchanged, and the units stay `%lthr`, so Intervals
+still converts from the LTHR it stores (172).
+
+## Colleague's note: what applied
+
+- **Applied:** `start`/`end` instead of `value`/`end` for the HR corridor. This
+  is the change above.
+- **Applied:** keep percentages with `%lthr` units, not absolute bpm. The
+  generator already did this; the note confirms the choice.
+- **Not applied:** the top-level `description` text grammar. `gen.py` does not
+  emit a `description`, and the watch problem does not depend on it. The
+  readback already shows `workout_doc.steps` populated, so the parser accepts
+  the event. Adding a description would be a separate change.
+- **Not applied:** building a test workout with the Intervals UI "Instant HR"
+  toggle. That was only a way to discover the key name, which the note has
+  already established.
+- **Not applied (not done here):** the push, read-back and watch-sync
+  verification. The ground rules say not to push or report to any external
+  service, so I have not sent anything to Intervals or Garmin.
+
+## Not verified
+
+- I have not confirmed on a real watch that `start`/`end` now shows
+  pct × 172 bpm. That needs a push, a Garmin sync and a check on the watch. The
+  claim rests on the colleague's single verified case and on the reading of
+  the symptom above.
+- `readback/event-184233-as-sent.json` still shows the old `value` shape. It is
+  a record of what was sent, so I left it as is.
+
+## To verify (next steps, when you choose to push)
+
+1. `python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json > event.json`, then `./push.sh event.json`.
+2. `GET /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/{new id}` and confirm the HR targets use
+   `start`/`end`.
+3. Sync Garmin Connect and open the workout. Expected: Warm-up 117–129 bpm,
+   Tempo 151–160, Float 129–141, Cool-down 112–124 (pct × 172). If the watch
+   still shows its own zone edges, the `start` key is not the cause.
